\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Exact event closure and the cost of a smaller description. Top (a): Bernoulli event total variation over four externally frozen independent four-event schedules at 81 prices. Exact hazard retains \(h_B(c)\) and reproduces the OR probability. The naive law uses \(\sigma (S_B-c)\). The common-intercept law uses the arithmetic mean of block-specific \(c_{\mathrm  {eff}}\) at each price. Its mean and maximum residuals quantify the effect of that restriction. The mean intercept minimises squared log-odds error, not TV. Bottom (b): for the same blocks, \(dc_{\mathrm  {eff}}/dc=\mathbb  E[N_B\mid N_B\geq 1]\). Curves give its block mean, minimum and maximum, with exact bounds 1 and 4. This is conditional event multiplicity, not an instability eigenvalue. The full margin schedules are retained for repricing. A single hazard value at one price is insufficient for that response.}}{14}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:num-toy-coarse-defect}{{6}{14}{Exact event closure and the cost of a smaller description. Top (a): Bernoulli event total variation over four externally frozen independent four-event schedules at 81 prices. Exact hazard retains \(h_B(c)\) and reproduces the OR probability. The naive law uses \(\sigma (S_B-c)\). The common-intercept law uses the arithmetic mean of block-specific \(c_{\mathrm {eff}}\) at each price. Its mean and maximum residuals quantify the effect of that restriction. The mean intercept minimises squared log-odds error, not TV. Bottom (b): for the same blocks, \(dc_{\mathrm {eff}}/dc=\mathbb E[N_B\mid N_B\geq 1]\). Curves give its block mean, minimum and maximum, with exact bounds 1 and 4. This is conditional event multiplicity, not an instability eigenvalue. The full margin schedules are retained for repricing. A single hazard value at one price is insufficient for that response}{figure.6}{}}
